tifies a `javax.crypto.Cipher.getInstance` overload with one or two arguments and the resulting Cipher object is the object followed by later rule events."},{"event":"Get","api_pattern":"javax.crypto.Cipher.getInstance(","matched_call":"getInstance","condition":"Observed: a local source match is a candidate factory call. Satisfies `Get` only when resolution identifies a `javax.crypto.Cipher.getInstance` overload with one or two arguments and the resulting Cipher object is the object followed by later rule events."},{"event":"Init","api_pattern":".init(","matched_call":"init","condition":"Observed: a call syntactically ending in `.init(`. Satisfies `Init` only when its resolved receiver is the tracked `javax.crypto.Cipher` and its signature is one of the modeled initialization overloads using a mode with a certificate or key, optionally parameters and/or `SecureRandom`."}],"detail":"the reviewed source contains a call the specification itself names as governed; the event's own condition text is quoted so its limits are read with it"},"caller_contract":{"status":"callers_enumerated","files_with_calls":3,"call_sites":4,"receiver_resolved_call_sites":4,"callers":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/EncryptedKeyTest.java","call_sites":[{"line":33,"receiver":"EncryptedKey","resolution":"repository_type","qualified_type":"org.fedorahosted.freeotp.encryptor.EncryptedKey","arity":2},{"line":48,"receiver":"EncryptedKey","resolution":"repository_type","qualified_type":"org.fedorahosted.freeotp.encryptor.EncryptedKey","arity":2}]},{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/MasterKey.java","call_sites":[{"line":45,"receiver":"EncryptedKey","resolution":"repository_type","qualified_type":"org.fedorahosted.freeotp.encryptor.EncryptedKey","arity":2}]},{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/Encryptor.java","call_sites":[{"line":56,"receiver":"EncryptedKey","resolution":"repository_type","qualified_type":"org.fedorahosted.freeotp.encryptor.EncryptedKey","arity":2}]}],"detail":"every file in the checkout that calls this name is listed"},"input_flow":{"status":"no_editable_text_parse","parse_calls":[],"unguarded_in_framework_callback":0,"bound":"Read from the reviewed method's text. An editable text widget can always yield an empty string, and a numeric inputType prevents neither that nor a value beyond the parser's range, so invalid input is feasible for a parse call fed straight from one. enclosed_by_try_that_catches is lexical: no try in this method catches a parse failure at that call. in_framework_callback means the call sits in a listener or on* callback the framework invokes, so no caller in the repository can handle its exception. validation_search, when present, is what a search of the repository's Java/Kotlin sources and layouts found for these widgets: validation calls that name them (watchers, filters, setError), an emptiness check in the method, the layout attributes of their view ids, the helpers they are passed to, and any global exception handler. no_validation_found_for_any_widget means none exists in the repository, so an empty field reaches the parse; widget_passed_to_helpers_that_may_validate and validation_found_for say what remains open. It does not read code generated at build time."},"byte_material":{"status":"no_byte_material_constructor","uses":[]},"parameter_producers":{"status":"collected","parameters":[{"parameter":"key","index":0,"passed_to":["cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key);"],"call_sites":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/MasterKey.java","line":45,"argument":"pwd","producers":[{"value":"pwd","produced_by":"skf.generateSecret(spec)","line":39},{"value":"skf","produced_by":"getSecretKeyFactory()","line":38,"which_returns":["SecretKeyFactory.getInstance("PBKDF2withHmacSHA512")","SecretKeyFactory.getInstance("PBKDF2withHmacSHA1")"]}],"status":"settled"},{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/Encryptor.java","line":56,"argument":"mk","producers":[{"value":"mk","produced_by":"mKeyStore.getKey(MASTER, null)","line":50},{"value":"mKeyStore","produced_by":"KeyStore.getInstance("AndroidKeyStore")","line":39}],"status":"settled"}]},{"parameter":"plaintext","index":1,"passed_to":["return new EncryptedKey(cipher, plaintext);"],"call_sites":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/MasterKey.java","line":45,"argument":"key","producers":[{"value":"key","produced_by":"new SecretKeySpec(raw, "AES")","line":43}],"status":"settled"},{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/Encryptor.java","line":56,"argument":"key","producers":[],"status":"not_settled"}]}],"bound":"call sites outside test sources, at most 40 files; producers follow plain assignments in the caller's file only"},"policy_evidence":{},"bound":"Derived from the checkout by deterministic rules, not by a model. A status of unresolved, undeclared_external, no_governed_api_matched or callers_truncated states a limit of what the checkout settles; it is not a negative finding. detector_reproduction alert_present means the detector that reported the finding raises the same rule in the same method on this revision; any other status there is a limit of what could be run, not evidence that the rule does not apply. byte_material fresh_zero_filled and constant_literal are facts about the bytes themselves: such bytes are fixed, the same on every run, and never the output of a random source; not_settled means the method and its file do not say. parameter_producers lists, for each parameter the method passes to a call, what every call site in the checkout passes and the assignments that produced it; when the method only forwards a value, the producers are where the governed value is made, and a fix belongs there. policy_evidence records what the pipeline itself observed outside the code -- connecting to a server, downloading a file and computing its digests -- and is established fact, not a hypothesis to confirm."},"diagnostic_evidence":{"evidence_id":"DET-001","kind":"detector_diagnostic","trust_level":"reported_detector_output","informational_only":true,"decision_authority":"none","sha256":"c25d86ba834c60b66cad545b2f0a73dccafec6b65ca81fe1728f656bf0505dd0","data":{"finding_id":"org.fedorahosted.freeotp.encryptor.EncryptedKey:::encrypt:::CipherSpec:::UnsatisfiedConstraint:::the key given to Cipher.init carries a key-origin predicate the rule does not admit","tool":"ares","specification":"CipherSpec","message":"the key given to Cipher.init carries a key-origin predicate the rule does not admit","reported_class":"org.fedorahosted.freeotp.encryptor.EncryptedKey","reported_method":"encrypt","source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKey.java","detector_context":{"code":"CIPHER-CONSTR-00","site_kind":"CONSTR: a value constraint was broken, or a required origin was positively contradicted","label":"violation","label_meaning":"A value check of the rule fired: an algorithm, key size, protocol, keystore type or other constraint outside what the rule admits, a required origin positively contradicted, or a forbidden call. The value seen and the admitted values are in value/expected.","expected":"a key produced by one of the generators the rule names","source_location":"EncryptedKey.java:42","runtime_observation":"Reported in 12 run(s) of the app; each run starts from a clean, read-only emulator."}}},"evidence_catalog":[{"evidence_id":"SRC-001","kind":"target_source","trust_level":"repository_exact_source","mandatory":true,"sha256":"aee29873bd16b40d3e046a8d211bcf53846536f39a41dfbe3156373e32527efe","data":{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKey.java","relevance":["reported finding location","constructs the reported class, deciding the state it reads","reviewed protected-value lifetime flow"],"content":"package org.fedorahosted.freeotp.encryptor;

import android.util.Log;

import java.io.IOException;
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;
import java.security.AlgorithmParameters;
import java.security.InvalidAlgorithmParameterException;
import java.security.InvalidKeyException;
import java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;

import javax.crypto.BadPaddingException;
import javax.crypto.Cipher;
import javax.crypto.IllegalBlockSizeException;
import javax.crypto.NoSuchPaddingException;
import javax.crypto.SecretKey;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;

public final class EncryptedKey {
    private final byte[] mCipherText;
    private final byte[] mParameters;
    private final String mCipher;
    private final String mToken;

    private EncryptedKey(Cipher cipher, SecretKey token)
            throws BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException {
        mCipher = cipher.getAlgorithm();
        mToken = token.getAlgorithm();

        cipher.updateAAD(mToken.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        mCipherText = cipher.doFinal(token.getEncoded());
        mParameters = cipher.getParameters().getEncoded();
    }

    public static EncryptedKey encrypt(SecretKey key, SecretKey plaintext)
            throws NoSuchAlgorithmException, NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeyException,
            BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException {
        if (key == null) {
            throw new InvalidKeyException("Key is null");
        }
        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding");
        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key);
        return new EncryptedKey(cipher, plaintext);
    }

    public SecretKey decrypt(SecretKey key)
            throws NoSuchPaddingException, NoSuchAlgorithmException, BadPaddingException,
            IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException, InvalidAlgorithmParameterException,
            InvalidKeyException {
        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(mCipher);
        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key);
        String algorithm = cipher.getParameters().getAlgorithm();

        AlgorithmParameters ap = AlgorithmParameters.getInstance(algorithm);
        ap.init(mParameters);

        cipher.init(Cipher.DECRYPT_MODE, key, ap);
        cipher.updateAAD(mToken.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        return new SecretKeySpec(cipher.doFinal(mCipherText), mToken);
    }
}
"}},{"evidence_id":"SPEC-001","kind":"verified_specification","trust_level":"verified_primary_specification","mandatory":true,"sha256":"586df8210d9991bf0a5d5396b355613c7709fb376495e6fb201b13b11cabfddd","data":{"status":"available","schema_version":2,"spec_id":"CipherSpec","name":"CipherSpec","applies_to_types":["javax.crypto.Cipher"],"source_title":"Cipher.crysl — CROSSINGTUD Crypto-API-Rules","source_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CROSSINGTUD/Crypto-API-Rules/refs/heads/master/JavaCryptographicArchitecture/src/Cipher.crysl","source_verified":true,"protocol":"Get, Init+, AADUpdate*, WKB+ | (FINWOU | (Update+, DoFinal))+","important_note":"Under the CrySL naming convention and the consulted rule's `SPEC javax.crypto.Cipher` declaration, CipherSpec governs `javax.crypto.Cipher`, not an application class or a namesake such as ESAPI's `org.owasp.esapi.crypto.CipherSpec`. The reported enclosing methods named `encrypt`, `decrypt`, and `create` do not establish a rule violation or prove which Cipher event occurred. This is a static protocol/predicate rule, not proof that a runtime operation is confidential, authentic, successful, or interoperable.","events":[{"name":"Get","api_patterns":["Cipher.getInstance(","javax.crypto.Cipher.getInstance("],"condition":"Observed: a local source match is a candidate factory call. Satisfies `Get` only when resolution identifies a `javax.crypto.Cipher.getInstance` overload with one or two arguments and the resulting Cipher object is the object followed by later rule events."},{"name":"Init","api_patterns":[".init("],"condition":"Observed: a call syntactically ending in `.init(`. Satisfies `Init` only when its resolved receiver is the tracked `javax.crypto.Cipher` and its signature is one of the modeled initialization overloads using a mode with a certificate or key, optionally parameters and/or `SecureRandom`."},{"name":"AADUpdate","api_patterns":[".updateAAD("],"condition":"Observed: a call syntactically ending in `.updateAAD(`. Satisfies `AADUpdate` only when its resolved receiver is the tracked Cipher and it is a byte-array, byte-array slice, or `ByteBuffer` overload; the rule further forbids this event for CTR, CTS, CFB, ECB, and OFB transformations."},{"name":"Update","api_patterns":[".update("],"condition":"Observed: a call syntactically ending in `.update(`. Satisfies `Update` only for a tracked Cipher and one of the modeled array or `ByteBuffer` overload forms; applicable offset and length predicates must also hold."},{"name":"DoFinal","api_patterns":[".doFinal("],"condition":"Observed: a call syntactically ending in `.doFinal(`. Satisfies `DoFinal` only for a modeled Cipher overload. `FINWOU` is the subset taking plaintext/input in the same call and is permitted as a one-shot final operation; zero-input/output finalization is modeled only after one or more `Update` events."},{"name":"WKB","api_patterns":[".wrap("],"condition":"Observed: a call syntactically ending in `.wrap(`. Satisfies `WKB` only when the resolved receiver is the tracked Cipher and bytes are produced by `Cipher.wrap(Key)` after required `Get` and `Init` events."}],"forbidden_inferences_without_evidence":["Do not infer that the reported `encrypt`, `decrypt`, or `create` methods directly invoke `javax.crypto.Cipher`; the output supplies enclosing names but no resolved invocation, receiver, or call path.","Do not infer that this rule governs `org.owasp.esapi.crypto.CipherSpec`, TLS CipherSpec terminology, or another type whose name merely ends in `Spec`.","Do not infer successful encryption, decryption, authentication, key wrapping, or absence of exceptions from a matching event sequence.","Do not infer GCM IV/nonce uniqueness, key entropy, key length, ciphertext transport, authentication-tag verification, or replay resistance solely from satisfaction of this rule.","Do not infer that every JCA- or Android-supported Cipher transformation is accepted by the rule; it uses a bounded transformation policy.","Do not infer the specific violated order, constraint, required predicate, or missing evidence from the representative message value `unknown`."],"semantic_scope":"The rule observes resolved uses of `javax.crypto.Cipher`: `getInstance`, selected `init` overloads, `updateAAD`, selected `update` and `doFinal` overloads, and `wrap`. It checks per-object event order, selected transformation/mode/padding and operation-mode constraints, buffer-bounds predicates, absence-of-call constraints, and CrySL typestate predicates including generated keys, randomized randomness, prepared parameters, and un-MACed plaintext. It does not model `Cipher.unwrap`, Cipher getters, provider-selection semantics beyond the two-argument factory event, or application-specific wrapper method names.","detector_semantics":{"claim":"For each tracked `javax.crypto.Cipher` object, the consulted CrySL rule requires a `Get` event followed by one or more `Init` events, optional AAD updates, and then either key wrapping or modeled finalization/streaming. It also applies stated transformation, mode, padding, type, range, and predicate constraints.","predicates":["`encmode` must be one of 1, 2, 3, or 4.","Public/private-key or certificate initialization implies RSA for wrap/unwrap modes 3 or 4; a `SecretKey` implies an allow-listed AES or PBE-with-AES algorithm.","AES is restricted to GCM, CTR, CTS, CFB, or OFB and requires `NoPadding`; RSA is restricted to no mode or ECB with the rule's listed padding values.","CTR, CTS, CFB, and OFB decryption/non-encryption modes may not use an init form without explicit IV/parameters; their encryption mode requires `preparedIV[paramSpec]`.","GCM requires `preparedGCM[paramSpec]`; listed OAEP padding cases require `preparedOAEP[paramSpec]`; `AlgorithmParameters` require `preparedAlg[params, alg(transformation)]`.","Key initialization requires one of `generatedKey[key, alg(transformation)]`, `generatedPubkey[key]`, or `generatedPrivkey[key]`; a supplied `SecureRandom` requires `rando